---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const description =
  "maws: what is running in an AWS account, what it costs per hour, and the month-to-date bill, in one terminal screen. Written in Mojo.";

const repo = "https://github.com/magmalake/maws";
const releases = `${repo}/releases`;
---

<Base title="maws" description={description}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow">Software</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">maws</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        What is running in my AWS account, what is it costing me per hour, and what have I
        been billed so far this month? One terminal screen, refreshed every minute, written
        in Mojo.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={repo} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn" href={releases} rel="noopener">Releases</a>
      </div>

      <figure class="shot">
        <a href="/s/maws/maws-tui.svg" aria-label="Open the screenshot full size">
        <img
          src="/s/maws/maws-tui.svg"
          width="1143"
          height="400"
          alt="The maws terminal UI: an account header, the burn rate per hour and per day, month-to-date and projected spend, a table of EC2 instances, NAT gateways, EBS volumes and Elastic IPs with their hourly cost, and the month-to-date bill by service."
          loading="lazy"
        />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Sample data, rendered by maws's own formatting code.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="cols">
        <div class="col">
          <h3>What it shows</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>$/hr</strong> for every running EC2 instance, EBS volume, NAT gateway and
              public IPv4 address, at the on-demand list price from the AWS Pricing API.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Month-to-date</strong> from Cost Explorer, by service, cached for an
              hour, since every call is billed at $0.01.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Projected</strong>: month-to-date plus the current burn for the rest of
              the month.
            </li>
            <li>The account name and ID, so a $0 for the wrong account is obvious.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <h3>How it is built</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              No AWS SDK and no C shim: requests are signed with
              <a href="https://github.com/magmalake/sigv4.mojo" rel="noopener">sigv4.mojo</a>,
              EC2's XML is read with
              <a href="https://github.com/magmalake/xml.mojo" rel="noopener">xml.mojo</a>, and
              libcurl is called directly from Mojo.
            </li>
            <li>
              Credentials from the environment, <code>~/.aws/credentials</code>, or the AWS
              CLI for <code>aws login</code>, SSO and role profiles.
            </li>
            <li>
              A Python reference (boto3 + Textual) in the same repository, held to the same
              numbers.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="install__head">Install</h3>
      <p class="install__text">
        Download the tarball for your platform (<code>macos-arm64</code> or
        <code>linux-x64</code>) from the <a href={releases} rel="noopener">releases page</a>,
        unpack it, and link <code>bin/maws</code> onto your <code>PATH</code>:
      </p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>v=0.1.0; p=macos-arm64
curl -fsSL "https://github.com/magmalake/maws/releases/download/v$v/maws-$v-$p.tar.gz" \
  | tar -C ~/.local/share -xz
ln -sf ~/.local/share/maws-$v-$p/bin/maws ~/.local/bin/maws
maws --profile my-profile</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .shot {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .shot figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .col {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
  }
  .col h3 {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.7rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .col ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }
  .col li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .col li::before {
    content: "+";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--lake);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .install__head {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }
  .install__text {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .install__code {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
